.UPDATE...
Issued at 927 AM PDT Tue Sep 8 2026

Want to emphasize that today will begin a warm-up that will peak
tomorrow, then moderate somewhat on Thursday with temperatures
closer to normal by Friday into the weekend. Even though todays
heat may not reach the level or extent necessary for an advisory,
it will still feel warmer than normal across much of our area,
including much our coastal areas that are experiencing a weak
fetch of offshore flow. Another factor adding to the heat concerns
tomorrow and Thursday, is the amount of moisture advecting north
with the remnants of Marie. Not only will we see higher
temperatures, we`ll see less relief overnight with the higher
dewpoints and higher relative humidity levels during peak heating
Wednesday and Thursday, further complicating heat impacts.
Remember to never leave people or pets in the car, take plenty of
breaks and seek shade/AC shelter if working outside and drink
plenty of people.

