.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 958 AM PDT Tue Sep 8 2026

Currently VFR at all terminals with stratus along the Big Sur
Coast and high clouds streaming in from the southwest. High
confidence in VFR through the TAF period, the only exception would
be if an eddy formed in the Monterey Bay or stratus developed off
the San Francisco Peninsula Coast. If clouds are able to form,
ceilings and visibilities would be LIFR. Diurnal winds will
prevail with a later than normal arrival of the sea breeze in the
afternoon. Winds will be light and likely variable overnight,
favoring terrain.

Vicinity of SFO...Currently VFR with light northeasterly flow.
High confidence in VFR through the TAF period. Diurnal winds will
prevail with a later than normal arrival of the sea breeze this
afternoon. Winds overnight may be light and variable, but will
likely favor a northeasterly direction.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Currently VFR with northwesterly flow at
MRY and VFR with drainage flow at SNS. Moderate to high confidence
in VFR prevailing through the TAF period, only exception would be
if an eddy is able to develop within the Bay. Diurnal winds will
prevail with a later than normal arrival of the sea breeze this
afternoon with drainage winds tonight.

